1. Naming Convention 

Variables, Components, CSS Class Names, Functions and Other Entities 

Use meaningful / descriptive names that reflect the purpose of the variable or function. 

Adhering naming conventions help maintain consistency and readability across the codebase, making it easier for developers to understand and collaborate on the code. 

Avoid abbreviations that may be unclear to others. 

Create concise yet descriptive names. 

